  "limitations": [
    "SCM tracking covers the native ARMv8 workers, not legacy SCM/other direct firmware calls; it is a conservative global hint, not synchronization.",
    "SCM can begin after the hint check. An accepted callback is always drained; there is no bounded completion timeout or guaranteed worst-case latency.",
    "Repeated failures/SCM skips retain previous governor data, potentially stale votes; benefit/power effects need measurement.",
    "Observed idle/isolated CPUs are not dispatched sampling IPIs, preserving native no-wakeup intent; a CPU can change state after selection, so this is not a no-wakeup race guarantee.",
    "Host mocks are sequential; no claim of real SMP, CPU-hotplug, perf-scheduling, firmware, suspend or runtime safety proof.",
    "Native AArch64 object/codegen only, not a complete image/modules link, boot or device/performance test.",
    "Shipped built-in miatoll configuration only: perf_event_read_local is not exported; existing governor registration functions are also unexported. Module linkage requires separate integration; no private helper export was added.",
    "ARM32 raw body preserved and C wrapper modeled, but no ARM32 target object compiled."
  ],
